=================== erc721.adoc
     1	= ERC-721
     2	
     3	We've discussed how you can make a _fungible_ token using xref:erc20.adoc[ERC-20], but what if not all tokens are alike?
     4	This comes up in situations like *real estate*, *voting rights*, or *collectibles*, where some items are valued more than others, due to their usefulness, rarity, etc.
     5	ERC-721 is a standard for representing ownership of xref:tokens.adoc#different-kinds-of-tokens[_non-fungible_ tokens], that is, where each token is unique.
     6	
     7	ERC-721 is a more complex standard than ERC-20, with multiple optional extensions, and is split across a number of contracts.
     8	The OpenZeppelin Contracts provide flexibility regarding how these are combined, along with custom useful extensions.
     9	Check out the https://docs.rs/openzeppelin-stylus/0.3.0/openzeppelin_stylus/token/erc721/struct.Erc721.html[`API reference`] to learn more about these.
    10	
    11	== Constructing an ERC-721 Token Contract
    12	
    13	We'll use ERC-721 to track items in our game, which will each have their own unique attributes.
    14	Whenever one is to be awarded to a player, it will be minted and sent to them.
    15	Players are free to keep their token or trade it with other people as they see fit, as they would any other asset on the blockchain!
    16	Please note any account can call `awardItem` to mint items.
    17	To restrict what accounts can be minted per item.
    18	We can use an xref:access-control.adoc[Access Control] extension.
    19	
    20	Here's what a contract for tokenized items might look like:
    21	
    22	[source,rust]
    23	----
    24	use openzeppelin_stylus::{
    25	    token::erc721::{
    26	        self,
    27	        extensions::{Erc721Metadata, IErc721Metadata},
    28	        Erc721, IErc721,
    29	    },
    30	    utils::introspection::erc165::IErc165,
    31	};
    32	
    33	#[entrypoint]
    34	#[storage]
    35	struct GameItem {
    36	    erc721: Erc721,
    37	    metadata: Erc721Metadata,
    38	    next_token_id: StorageU256,
    39	}
    40	
    41	#[public]
    42	#[implements(IErc721<Error = Error>, IErc721Metadata<Error = erc721::Error>, IErc165)]
    43	impl GameItem {
    44	    #[constructor]
    45	    fn constructor(&mut self, name: String, symbol: String, base_uri: String) {
    46	        self.metadata.constructor(name, symbol);
    47	        self.metadata.base_uri.set_str(base_uri);
    48	    }
    49	
    50	    fn award_item(&mut self, player: Address) -> Result<U256, erc721::Error> {
    51	        let token_id = self.next_token_id.get() + uint!(1_U256);
    52	        self.next_token_id.set(token_id);
    53	
    54	        self.erc721._mint(player, token_id)?;
    55	
    56	        Ok(token_id)
    57	    }
    58	}
    59	
    60	#[public]
    61	impl IErc721 for GameItem {
    62	    type Error = erc721::Error;
    63	
    64	    fn balance_of(&self, owner: Address) -> Result<U256, Self::Error> {
    65	        self.erc721.balance_of(owner)
    66	    }
    67	
    68	    fn owner_of(&self, token_id: U256) -> Result<Address, Self::Error> {
    69	        self.erc721.owner_of(token_id)
    70	    }
    71	
    72	    fn safe_transfer_from(
    73	        &mut self,
