   151	
   152	The https://docs.rs/openzeppelin-stylus/0.3.0/openzeppelin_stylus/token/erc721/extensions/metadata/struct.Erc721Metadata.html[`Erc721Metadata`] contract is an extension contract of ERC-721.
   153	It extends the contract itself with the name, symbol and base uri for the token.
   154	
   155	Also note that, unlike ERC-20, ERC-721 lacks a `decimals` field, since each token is distinct and cannot be partitioned.
   156	
   157	For more information about erc721 schema, check out the https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-721[ERC-721 specification].
   158	
   159	NOTE: You'll notice that the item's information is included in the metadata, but that information isn't on-chain!
   160	So a game developer could change the underlying metadata, changing the rules of the game!
   161	
   162	[[erc721-token-extensions]]
   163	== Extensions
   164	
   165	Additionally, there are multiple custom extensions, including:
   166	
   167	* xref:erc721-burnable.adoc[ERC-721 Burnable]: A way for token holders to burn their own tokens.
   168	
   169	* xref:erc721-consecutive.adoc[ERC-721 Consecutive]: An implementation of https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-2309[ERC2309] for minting batches of tokens during construction, in accordance with ERC721.
   170	
   171	* xref:erc721-enumerable.adoc[ERC-721 Enumerable]: Optional extension that allows enumerating the tokens on chain, often not included since it requires large gas overhead.
   172	
   173	* xref:erc721-metadata.adoc[ERC-721 Metadata]: Optional extension that adds name, symbol, and token URI, almost always included.
   174	
   175	* xref:erc721-pausable.adoc[ERC-721 Pausable]: A primitive to pause contract operation.
   176	
   177	* xref:erc721-uri-storage.adoc[ERC-721 Uri Storage]: A more flexible but more expensive way of storing metadata.
   178	
   179	* xref:erc721-wrapper.adoc[ERC-721 Wrapper]: Wrapper to create an ERC-721 backed by another ERC-721, with deposit and withdraw methods.
